From: "Piotr P. Karwasz" <piotr@github.copernik.eu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:25:59 +0100
Subject: Generate CycloneDX 1.7 SBOMs for the source tree and the
 build

Add two make targets:

- "make source-sbom" writes apr-source.cdx.json, describing the source
  tree: all third-party code it contains and every external library
  the UNIX build may link against, with the range of versions accepted.
  Its purpose is mostly license compliance.

- "make sbom" writes apr.cdx.json, describing this build: the external
  libraries libapr needs at run time, read from the DT_NEEDED entries of
  the built shared library (or the -l flags it was linked with), with
  the versions found on the build system and the files they resolved
  to, so that packagers can map them to their packages.  Third-party
  code is listed only when it comes from a maintained upstream whose
  advisories could apply; code forked long ago is only of interest for
  license compliance and is left to the source SBOM.

build/sbom.sh does the work, with jq.  It reads the components from
build/sbom/components.json, while licenses and copyrights of
third-party code come from the SPDX tags in the source files.  It fails
if a file carries a license tag other than Apache-2.0 that
components.json does not account for.

The output is reproducible: the timestamp comes only from
SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH, the serial number is a version 5 UUID derived from
the package URL, and the script runs with LC_ALL=C.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Forwarded: no
